Atari Quake
https://github.com/agranlund/quake

Based on Atari Quake 1.00 by mikrosk
https://github.com/mikrosk/quake


This work in progress port attempts to add support for non Falcon hardware.

Changes:
- NOVA graphics card support
- Do not use STe/Falcon DMA sound when not available
- Reduced heapsize to 8mb (16mb when there is 24mb or more free)
- Keyboard and mouse on machines without a real IKBD ACIA (Raven060,
  EmuTOS clones) through the TOS 2.0+ kbdvec / mousevec vectors
- Keyboard and video are restored if the game exits with an error
- Sound Blaster output on ISA machines (Raven060) without DMA: MFP
  Timer A plays 8-bit mono at ~11kHz, as in pmdoom. -nosb disables it.

Input options:
  (default)   Falcon/TT: original ACIA handler, everything else: kbdvec
  -kbdvec     force the TOS kbdvec/mousevec handler (needs TOS 2.0+/EmuTOS)
  -ikbd       force the original ACIA handler
  -noinput    no keyboard/mouse hooks (self running demo only)
  -nomouse    keyboard only
  -mouselook  always use the mouse to look around
  -mem <mb>   heap size in megabytes

Issues:
- Sound needs Falcon DMA sound or a Sound Blaster compatible ISA card.
- Run it from plain TOS/EmuTOS. Under MiNT with memory protection the
  input handlers can not be called from the keyboard interrupt.


Usage:
Copy the Quake PAK files into the ID1 folder and run quake.ttp

  Shareware (episode 1):  ID1\PAK0.PAK
  Full version:           ID1\PAK0.PAK and ID1\PAK1.PAK

The full version needs PAK1.PAK from your own copy of Quake (the
original CD, Steam or GOG releases all contain it, in the id1 folder).
With the 2021 Steam/GOG release use the original files from Quake\id1,
not the ones in the "rerelease" folder: those need a newer engine.
Original v1.06 sizes: PAK0.PAK 18,689,235 bytes, PAK1.PAK 34,257,856.
Once PAK1.PAK is present the console shows "Playing registered version"
and all four episodes are available. The shareware PAK0.PAK and the
full version PAK0.PAK are the same file.
